module bindings.php.resolveFailureUrlValidationBypass;

// PHP documents gethostbyname() as returning "the IPv4 address of the
// Internet host specified by hostname or a string containing the unmodified
// hostname on failure". A URL validator that hands the host to the resolver
// therefore learns two things from the call: the address, or -- by comparing
// the answer with the input -- that the name did not resolve. The second
// case is the one a fetch gate has to fail closed on: a host string the
// resolver would not interpret is exactly the string an HTTP client may
// still interpret on its own, and cURL's address parser accepts hex, octal
// and short integer spellings of `127.0.0.1` that glibc's gethostbyname()
// rejects outright. A validator that records the failure by assigning a bare
// `false` back to the resolved variable and then continues -- so the range
// test that follows is skipped by its own truthiness guard and the function
// still reaches its accept return -- passes such hosts as safe, and the
// request that follows connects to an internal address the validator never
// saw (CWE-918).
//
// The discriminator has to correlate two assignments on the same variable:
// the resolution (`$ip = gethostbyname($host)`) and the falsy sentinel
// (`$ip = false`), with the documented failure comparison between them. A
// presence clause cannot unify a variable across two tokens, and an
// uncorrelated false literal in the same function -- a same-host flag, a
// status default -- satisfies it just as well, on the patched revision too.
// The PHP review extractor performs the correlation and emits
// `resolve_failure_url_validation_bypass`; this binding only turns that fact
// into the issue. A validator that rejects the failure with `die()`, `exit()`
// or a `return` does not reset the resolved variable, and one that routes
// the answer through filter_var() rejects the unmodified-hostname failure
// return itself, so neither is matched. The residual is a function that
// resets the resolved variable and rejects on it in a later branch; nothing
// in the measured reachable set spells it that way.
binding gethostbynameFailureSentinelNotRejected {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "php" and node.context.phpReview == "resolve_failure_url_validation_bypass"
  emit issue code.ResolveFailureUrlValidationBypass at node
}
